## Q8 (gui-stack-v1-issues) — self-referential class types. Before the fix
## these crashed the COMPILER with a stack overflow: the structural
## auto-derive check (typeck) and the layout/size computation (codegen)
## both recursed through the self-reference with no cycle detection. A
## class instance is a heap pointer, so `Array[Node]` / `Option[Node]` are
## representable; cycle detection now terminates both walks (coinductive /
## pointer-sized on a cycle). Covers a container self-ref AND a direct
## Option self-ref, with field access through the recursion.

class Node
  label: String
  children: Array[Node]
  next: Option[Node]
  def init(@label: String)
    self.children = Array.new
    self.next = nil
  end
end

def main
  var root = Node.new(String.from("root"))
  root.children.push(Node.new(String.from("kid1")))
  root.children.push(Node.new(String.from("kid2")))
  puts "kids: #{root.children.size}"
  if let Some(first) = root.children.get(0)
    puts "first: #{first.label}"
  end

  root.next = Some(Node.new(String.from("sibling")))
  match root.next
    Some(n) -> puts "next: #{n.label}"
    nil     -> puts "next: none"
  end
end
